comments.body:
@participant2 I figured out your issue. I got the clue from #1983 as the addition for `MSYS_NO_PATHCONV` checks for the following `has('win32unix')`. It is only true in the version of `vim` that comes with git bash (and probably with cygwing as per the help description). I found that I have `neovim` and `vim` from scoop higher in my path which return false to that feature check but they return true to `has('win32')`.

If I load fzf and fzf.vim in the vim from git bash it does what you describe, it goes directly into cmd.exe.
Could you try downloading neovim (to avoid confusion with vim) and try there? If `has('win32unix')` is false, it should work fine.
